notes.body:
pcaps for DHCPv6 DNR options: and DNS SVCB records:

[dhcpv6_dnr_packets.pcapng](/uploads/9f5f5b5a8bedb2f2406e166223c6db9f/dhcpv6_dnr_packets.pcapng)

[dns_svcb_packets.pcapng](/uploads/4c0dee2f6d1ad9c394af9637c0682afc/dns_svcb_packets.pcapng)

DHCPv6 DNR old (retail 4.4.9):

![image.png](/uploads/2a6350993a713a6b9dc0f89859de5434/image.png){width="286" height="252"}

DHCPv6 DNR new:

![image.png](/uploads/ee4ba4adde5fed4dfec0db9f6be2471c/image.png){width="409" height="662"}

DNS SVCB records new (unchanged from old):

![image.png](/uploads/a4bd089d1d07092ffd2a2aa652152f9a/image.png){width="407" height="481"}

I've updated the code to use the PINO logic that I could find (registering with proto_register_protocol_in_name_only, using call_dissector in other dissectors). Now the SVC params appear under their own top level filter like "svc_params.port":

DHCPv6:

![image.png](/uploads/5c7d88e6246d1b84fc7e748c144a1d86/image.png){width=334 height=480}

DNS:

![image.png](/uploads/2f75d1bb599444fafde3d951de6e9178/image.png){width=410 height=480}

